    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-California/Project-Manager--Nurse-Practitioner_R20263524-2": {
      "title": "Family Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $106,020.00 - $158,000.00 Compensation : $106,020 to $158,000 USD annually Project Manager Family Nurse Practitioner (Grant-Funded) The Dr. Gloria J. McNeal Nurse Managed Clinic (GJMNMC) Based in San Diego Are you a mission-driven Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) passionate about serving vulnerable and underserved communities? Join the Dr. Gloria J. McNeal Nurse Managed Clinic and help expand access to high-quality healthcare for individuals and families who need it most. This is an exciting opportunity to combine clinical practice, program leadership, community outreach, and grant-funded healthcare initiatives while making a meaningful impact across Southern California. Please Note: This is a grant-funded position currently funded through June 30, 2027 . This position includes travel to Los Angeles as needed About the Role The Project Manager Family Nurse Practitioner (PMFNP) provides both clinical and operational leadership for the Dr. Gloria J. McNeal Nurse Managed Clinic's community-based healthcare programs. The selected candidate will oversee clinic operations, supervise healthcare personnel, support grant initiatives, and deliver direct patient care to underserved populations. This role serves individuals experiencing health disparities, including people experiencing homelessness and other at-risk populations , while also supporting healthcare services provided in community settings, including elementary schools . Candidates must possess Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) certification and have experience providing care across the lifespan. Location & Travel Candidates must reside in San Diego, CA Frequent travel between clinic and community sites within the candidate's assigned region is required Travel expenses are reimbursed Ability and willingness to travel up to 75% to support clinic operations, outreach initiatives, and grant-related activities What You'll Do Clinical & Community Care Deliver primary care services to underserved and vulnerable populations Provide healthcare services to individuals experiencing homelessness and other at-risk populations Support community-based healthcare initiatives throughout Los Angeles and San Diego Deliver care within mobile, community, and school-based settings Collaborate with interdisciplinary healthcare teams to improve patient outcomes Monitor patient care plans and support continuity of care Clinic Operations & Leadership Manage day-to-day operations across multiple clinic locations Oversee clinic workflows, scheduling, and patient-centered service delivery Supervise Nurse Practitioners and Community Health Administration staff Support billing, credentialing, compliance, and quality improvement initiatives Manage Electronic Health Record systems and operational processes Ensure culturally responsive and high-quality care delivery Grant & Program Management Support all grant-funded initiatives and compliance requirements Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders to achieve project goals Assist with federal reporting, outcome tracking, and data collection Support budget monitoring and grant deliverables Partner with community organizations to expand access to care Community Outreach Build relationships with community agencies, schools, and service organizations Represent the clinic at community events and health fairs Support initiatives that increase healthcare access for underserved populations Required Qualifications Education Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) required Doctoral degree in Nursing, Healthcare, or related field preferred Licensure & Certification Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) certification required Current and unencumbered Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) Certification and Registered Nurse (RN) Licensure required. Active California furnishing number, National Provider Identifier (NPI), and DEA registration number required. Maintain current national and state board certification as a Nurse Practitioner from an approved organization such as: American Nurses Credentialing Center (ANCC) American Academy of Nurse Practitioners (AANP) National Certification Corporation (NCC) for Obstetrics, Gynecologic, and Neonatal Nursing Specialties Experience Minimum 5 years of healthcare leadership or management experience Experience serving underserved, vulnerable, or historically marginalized populations Experience managing healthcare programs, clinical teams, or community-based services Experience with grant-funded healthcare programs preferred Pediatric experience required , as the role includes providing care within elementary school settings Experience working with communities experiencing homelessness strongly preferred Preferred Qualifications Federal grant management experience Nurse faculty or preceptor experience Experience working with community-based organizations and public health initiatives Experience supporting behavioral health and primary care integration Why Join Us? This role offers a unique opportunity to: Improve healthcare access for vulnerable populations Help shape innovative community-based healthcare programs Lead multidisciplinary teams across Southern California Support both clinical excellence and meaningful community impact Contribute to a federally funded initiative focused on health equity and access If you are a compassionate Family Nurse Practitioner who is passionate about community health, healthcare equity, and serving those most in need, we encourage you to apply and help make a lasting difference across Los Angeles and San Diego communities. #LI-On-site Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
