    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Part-time-Advanced-Practice-Nurse_R20253145": {
      "title": "Part-time Advanced Practice Nurse",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-01-06\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $60.00 - $65.00 National University’s School of Health Professions, in collaboration with the School of Education, invites applications for a uniquely rewarding Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) position within a long-term, grant-funded initiative serving elementary school communities across San Diego. This role is ideal for an FNP who values meaningful patient interaction, interdisciplinary teamwork, and community-centered care. You will join a highly collaborative, close-knit group of healthcare professionals who are passionate about equitable access, preventive care, and whole-family wellbeing. Position Highlights Part-time, flexible scheduling: Work two-three days per week, Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday. Family-centered clinical practice: Provide care not only to elementary school students, but also to their parents and siblings. a rare opportunity to support holistic family health in a school-based setting. Low daily patient volume: Typically 5–8 patients per day (with the higher end occurring infrequently), allowing for 45-minute visits and the ability to deliver thorough, relationship-based care. Integrated health education: When clinic volume is lower, engage with students in the classroom, teaching preventive care, mental health awareness, and the relationship between physical and emotional wellbeing. Community impact: Participate in one Saturday Community Health Fair per month on a rotating basis, as well as occasional after-school community events. Weekly hours flex accordingly—for example, working two 4-hour days during the same week to accommodate Saturday or after-school coverage. Hybrid work potential: On-site coverage from 8:00–8:45 a.m. start time through  3:00 p.m. , with remaining hours available to be completed remotely. Grant-funded stability: Funding is secured through 2029, offering long-term consistency within a mission-driven program. What Makes This Role Special A supportive team environment with strong communication, shared resources, and a true commitment to community health. The ability to practice at a thoughtful pace, building real relationships with families. A balanced clinical and educational scope that enables you to influence health literacy from an early age. A schedule that supports work–life balance and flexibility. Requirements: Education & Experience: Graduate of an accredited school of nursing with an earned Master of Science in nursing degree. Graduate of an accredited Nurse Practitioner Program. Current Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) Certification and Licensure as a Registered Nurse. Current California Furnishing number, NPI and current DEA registration number. Hold and maintain current national and state board certification as a nurse practitioner from approved organization (American Nurses Credentialing Center, American Academy of Nurse Practitioner, National Certification Corporation for Obstetrics, Gynecologic and Neonatal Nursing Specialty). Current certification in Basic Life Support (BLS), Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS), and PALS. Recent experience in an advanced practice nurse role. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Publisher, Outlook, SharePoint, Adobe and Peoplesoft. Knowledge of office policies and procedures, and strong organizational skills. Strong interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequently changing priorities. Strong analytical skills and attention to detail and accuracy. Demonstrated interpersonal skills to work cooperatively with diverse individuals; proven ability to communicate professionally. Works well independently, possesses the ability to take direction, work as a team player, and maintain confidentiality. Location: Onsite at designated school site locations. Travel: Up to 75% travel to ensure clinical practice consistency across all clinic locations. #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Veteran-Education-Benefits-Assistant---VA-Work-Study_R20263489-1": {
      "title": "Veteran Education Benefits Assistant – VA Work Study",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: : $16.90 - $16.90 Position Summary The Veteran Education Benefits Assistant supports National University’s (NU) School Certifying Official (SCO) team in providing accurate and timely assistance to students using Veterans Education Benefits. They will work closely with SCO team leadership to identify military-affiliated student needs and participate in campus initiatives that support Veteran Services (e.g., Veteran Center Food Pantry). The VEB Assistant will attend webinars, student orientations, and on-campus training seminars related to VA Education Benefits. Additional responsibilities may include other tasks related to on-campus Veteran Services as assigned. Location:  Hybrid, Spectrum Center, San Diego, CA Essential Functions: Fields Veteran Education Benefits inquiries in person, by phone, and virtually. Assists with reporting student enrollments to the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. Process VA correspondence and support other administrative tasks related to the administration of Veteran Education Benefits. Perform other duties as assigned to support the effective delivery of on-campus Veteran Services. Requirements: Current NU student receiving Veteran Education Benefits under Title 38, U.S.C., Chapters 30, 31, 32, 33, 35, 1606, and Edith N. Rogers STEM Scholarship. Enrolled in and pursuing an approved program of education at a rate of 3/4 time or greater during the work study semester. Maintain good academic standing according to NU’s Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) Policy. Ability to meet National University’s employee performance and campus dress code standards. Experience in customer service and customer relations. Technical / Functional Skills : Fundamental understanding of Veterans Education Benefits. Ability to navigate VA.gov, Ask VA, eBenefits.gov, and the GI Bill® Comparison Tool. Proficiency in communicating within hybrid work environments. Basic computer skills with experience using Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to complete projects in a timely manner. Note :   Veterans with service-connected disabilities rated at 30 percent or more are given hiring priority for VA Work Study positions. #LI-DNI   Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Veteran-and-Military-Community-Center-Assistant---VA-Work-Study--Spectrum-Center--San-Diego--CA-_R20263490-1": {
      "title": "Veteran and Military Community Center Assistant – VA Work Study (Spectrum Center, San Diego, CA)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: : $16.90 - $16.90 Position Summary The Veteran & Military Community Center Assistant works in the Veteran & Military Community Center within the Campus Operations department. They provide support to the VMCC Associate Director, VMCC Coordinator, School Certifying Officials, and Veteran/Military Students and/or their dependents by assisting Veteran students with general inquiries about Veteran benefits, Veteran’s activities, and assisting with outreach. They may attend webinars, student orientations, and on-campus training seminars related to VA Education Benefits. Additional responsibilities may include other tasks related to on-campus Veteran Services as assigned. Location:  Onsite Spectrum Center, San Diego, CA Essential Functions: Answers phone calls, directs students on campus and over the phone, sends and receives emails and answers questions to walk-in students. Assists Veteran students with general inquiries about Veteran benefits they can receive on and off campus, Veteran’s activities, directing students to other student support service locations at the University. Assists and participates in outreach within the community and with on-campus efforts and events. Collects, compiles, and tracks data in support of the Veteran & Military Community Center . Performs basic data analysis and generates reports. Conducts other clerical, office duties as required. Maintains positive relationships with student support departments, in order to facilitate services to students receiving Veteran-related educational entitlements. Assists with the development and distribution of accurate and current Veterans publications to relevant constituencies (brochures, flyers, posters and web content). Assists with maintaining regulatory, information security and confidentiality compliance in accordance with federal, state and NU guidelines. Maintains most current information and updates by attending required trainings to support VMCC Assoc. Director, VMCC Coordinator, School Certifying Officials, and Veteran/Military Students. Requirements: Current NU student receiving Veteran Education Benefits under Title 38, U.S.C., Chapters 30, 31, 32, 33, 35, 1606, and Edith N. Rogers STEM Scholarship. Enrolled in and pursuing an approved program of education at a rate of 3/4 time or greater during the work study semester. Maintain good academic standing according to NU’s Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) Policy. Ability to meet National University’s employee performance and campus dress code standards. Experience in customer service and customer relations. Technical / Functional Skills: Fundamental understanding of Veterans Education Benefits. Basic computer skills with experience using Microsoft Office Suite. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to complete projects in a timely manner. Note:   Veterans with service-connected disabilities rated at 30 percent or more are given hiring priority for VA Work Study positions. #LI-DNI   Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
