    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Full-time-Assistant-Professor-in-Clinical-Mental-Health_R20263549": {
      "title": "Full-time Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $66,560.00 - $75,066.00 National University – San Diego, California Assistant Professor in Clinical Mental Health – Remote, USA The Department of Counseling Psychology and Social Work, in the John F. Kennedy School of Psychology and Social Sciences at National University, invites applications for an Assistant Professor in the Clinical Mental Health program. Rank is commensurate with qualifications and experience . The successful candidate will have the potential for excellence in teaching and scholarship in the counseling field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position is remote. This position works closely with other faculty within the discipline and administration contributing to programmatic strategies that ensure program quality, student engagement, and success. We are looking for a candidate who can collaborate with faculty, program leadership, and operations staff to support the delivery of comprehensive, high-quality academic and clinical training experience for students. While the primary function of this role is teaching and requires the ability to teach across various courses, it also integrates service, scholarship, and clinical training experience to support student development and program excellence. The Assistant Professor reports to the Department Chair and works closely with CMHC leadership to ensure alignment with programmatic goals and accreditation standards, including those established by CACREP. Essential Functions Candidates will be evaluated for their level of proficiency and potential (for excellence) in teaching, scholarship, and service. The main expectations of this position include: Teaching Teach and develop online courses in the area of clinical mental health in content areas of counseling theories, assessment and testing, and diagnosis and treatment. Teach clinical courses and participate in Final Presentations. Maintain pedagogical and subject matter expertise in the instructor’s field. Create an inclusive and positive learning environment for diverse learners. Ensure course and program practices align with compliance and accreditation standards. Adhere to the National University’s academic integrity policy. Scholarship Maintain a productive scholarship agenda suitable to a teaching university. Engage in scholarly activities to maintain professional growth with counseling organizations such as the American Counseling Association. Participate in professional development as outlined in faculty policies. Service Support school and program leadership on accreditation reviews. Consult on program processes and participate in discussions to improve and innovate the CMHC program. Provide regular opportunities to offer academic guidance and mentorship to individual CMHC students on training process and placements, program requirements, development of practicum and career goals, and any problems/concerns that they encounter throughout the tenor of their program. Participates in any remediation processes involving CMHC students. Serve as a reviewer of all program materials to ensure compliance with CACREP and state standards. Collaborate and provide support to internal stakeholders on appropriate data collection, analysis, evaluation, and dissemination of reports including the regular evaluation of the students’ comportment and experience quality. Serve a faculty advisor for student organizations such as CSI and faculty point of contact for student programming such as new student orientation, graduation celebration, etc. Maintain professional communication with internal and external stakeholders. Participate in administrative meetings and project teams as requested. Complete all other tasks and/or projects as assigned.  Maintain membership and actively participate with professional counseling organizations such as the American Counseling Association. The ideal candidate will possess the following qualifications : Education & Experience Doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited institution/program required. Licensed or license eligible as a professional counselor (LPC) required. Strong identification with professional counselor identity and evidence of such, e.g., membership in professional counselor organization(s), licensing activities, conference attendance, etc., required. 2+ years of faculty experience in a program in a CACREP accredited CMHC program and/or clinical training administration experience in a CACREP accredited CMHC program preferred. Experience with CACREP accreditation and compliance as well as ability to assist in management of such preferred Experience teaching online courses in asynchronous format; experience working in a technology-driven enterprise preferred. Curriculum development experience preferred. Special conditions of employment include: Background check required. Travel is required at least once annually to attend the annual Commencement ceremony (if held onsite). For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter that includes interest in the position and brief summary of required qualifications met. A curriculum vita Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/MultiUse-Lab-Assistant-Supervisor--Spectrum-Center-_R20263574": {
      "title": "MultiUse Lab Assistant Supervisor (Spectrum Center)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $20.00 - $25.77 Position Summary Assist the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director in the overseeing of the Multiuse laboratories in support of National University academic programs.  Provides technical support to the Mulituse laboratories at the campuses. Work closely with university staff, faculty and students to ensure a positive teaching and learning experience. Under the supervision of the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor ensure compliance with OSHA / EPA / California regulations and safety requirements. Assist with supervision, training, and coordination of the work schedule of the Multiuse Laboratory Assistant(s) and/or Technician(s). Maintains a positive team environment, leading the team when the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director is not present, providing reporting and class preparation support for team members, driving results, and coaching to outcomes for the team. In addition, is the first point of contact for students and organizational escalations. Essential Functions Act as the auxiliary supervisor for all Multiuse Laboratories within the National University System. Supervise the preparations for laboratory experiments and demonstrations for scheduled classes in close collaboration with university faculty. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff on experiment set-ups. Assist instructors and students during laboratory classes. Provide monthly and long-term laboratory schedules to campus directors, SoALS and resolve scheduling conflicts. Develop a hands-on operating guide for the SeqStudio genetic analyzer, and keep it updated when forensic procedures change. Develop a hands-on operating guide for the Ultra Performance Liquid Chromatography (UPLC) for chemical separation and analysis.    Add procedures for confirmatory testing of when chemical materials are added to the forensic curriculum.    Provide guidance to Facilities, SoALS, and Campus Operations on laboratory design/workflow when new laboratories are added or when existing laboratories are updated. Guidance could include equipment lists, pricing, water/electrical requirements, laboratory safety equipment requirements, and storage requirements. Follow policies and procedures for good laboratory practices. Maintain consumable and perishable components to OSHA / EPA standards. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff and instructors on experiment set-ups and outcomes. Assist with and train multiuse laboratory staff, professors, and students in the proper disposal of HAZMAT / BIOHAZ materials. Train multiuse laboratory staff on the Medical Waste Management Plan, SDS use and maintenance, chemical storage, and inventories, chemical and bio-hazardous disposal, logs, and laboratory safety, I.A.W, National University policies. Ensure multiuse laboratory staff understand and comply with the proper handling and storage of hazardous materials and human pathogens per OSHA / EPA regulations and standards. Ensure the laboratory is maintained in good working order. Emphasis on neatness, cleanliness, stocked reagents bottles, and all equipment is in good working order. Perform depot level maintenance on all microscopes, clean lenses, correct adjustment on ocular lenses, clean & align condenser, repair stage, and change light assembly. Perform periodic maintenance on SeqStudio Genetic analyzer, Polaris Q mass spectrophotometer (MS), Trace gas chromatograph (GC), and UPLC per the manufacturer’s guidelines.  Contact the manufacturer if warranty repairs are needed. Order, store, and maintain a current and complete inventory of laboratory supplies. Replenish stock, as needed.  Export packaged courses to other university campuses. Manage projects and deadlines set by the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director to ensure timely progression and completion. Provide team member training support. Identify current team and individual challenges to provide early intervention for team member improvement.  Maintain team member coaching log and provide feedback to Associate Director for annual evaluations and regular 1:1s. Provide escalation support and first level conflict resolution.  Lead department meetings. Hold 1:1s with team members and provide skills coaching. Team oversight and coverage support in the absence of the Multiuse Laboratory Supervisor and/or Director Remediation committee team member for performance management. Maintain the highest level of integrity and professionalism. Coach and provide feedback for team members on lab and chemical preparation and safety Support front line team members through safety changes as well as course changes and all things involved with being able to teach those courses Oversee team member engagement in class as necessary when expectations are not being met. Provide support and coverage for team as needed. Participate in ongoing department projects, or other special projects, as needed. Reasonable and consistent attendance to fulfill requirements of the position. Other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities :   Indirect oversight of up to 6 front line team members. Coaching, performance support and feedback, outcome delivery, process management, and team member training required. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree in science-related field of study required; and, two to four (2-4) years of experience in science laboratory techniques and concepts in the areas of life, physical, and forensics sciences, safety regulations and procedures in science laboratories. Manage teams of technicians at the Spectrum, South Bay, Naval Hospital, Fresno, and Los Angeles locations. Provide lab technicians training on the operation and maintenance of all laboratory equipment using written, Zoom sessions, and onsite visits. Provide training on Aseptic techniques, bacterial culturing, and sterile bacterial media preparation to all technicians. Ensure technicians know how to interpret course syllabi and laboratory schedules to provide timely laboratory preparation and setups. Operation and maintenance of SeqStudio Genetic Analysis, UPLC chromatography, PCR, electrophoresis, physiology workstations, microscopes, FT-IR and UV-VIS spectrophotometry. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Ability to effectively and efficiently communicate organizational goals and deadlines to team members. Ability to create a positive and productive work environment. Ability to provide support in the hiring and training process of new team members. Ability to coach to skill improvement and outcome development. Strong understanding of all degree programs, specializations, and courses. Ability to stay current via self-study on university policies, including policy update In-depth knowledge of science laboratory procedures, safety and chemical hygiene plans and small spill clean-up. Ability to conduct internet search and requisition for laboratory supplies, chemicals, and equipment. Strong understanding of Natural Science and science laboratory operations/vernacular. Strong written and verbal skills, organization, and follow-through. Attention to detail. Ability to use science laboratory tools and equipment required to support a typical university level academic environment/curriculum. Function as university laboratory operations and safety expert and achieve compliance with external and internal safety policies and procedures. Achieve compliance with regulations regarding storage/use/disposal of HAZMAT and BIOHAZ material. Establish new vendor contracts and maintain current vendor agreements and warranties. Solves problems and develops relationships through shared goal of providing optimum learning environment for university students. Ability to participate as an active team member of the team and organization and work toward a common goal. Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company and oneself. Work independently and foster a cooperative spirit within a large and/or small team of diverse cultures, while working in a fast-paced environment with multiple projects, deadlines, and frequently changing priorities. Location: Onsite, Spectrum Center Travel: May be required to other National University campuses with a multiuse laboratory and other areas to assess new locations for a laboratory.   #LI-Onsite Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Payroll-Manager--Contractor-_R20263560-1": {
      "title": "Payroll Manager (Contractor)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $40.00 - $50.00 Position Summary The Payroll Manager is responsible for overseeing the daily multi-state payroll operations for a large organization and ensuring the accurate and timely processing of payroll.  This position requires close collaboration with the Human Resources and Finance departments to maintain data integrity, reconcile payroll transactions, and support organizational goals. The Payroll Manager ensures compliance with all applicable local, state, federal, and international tax laws and wage regulations, addressing pay-related issues and supporting both staff and leadership.  The Payroll Manager maintains data integrity, reconciles payroll transactions, manages payroll vendors and systems, and translates organizational priorities into reliable payroll operations. Essential Functions: Supervises, mentors, and supports payroll staff by providing training, guidance, and performance feedback. Manages end-to-end payroll processing, ensuring accurate and timely preparation of weekly, biweekly, and monthly payrolls. Ensures compliance with federal, state, and local payroll regulations, including oversight of W-2 preparation and year-end tax reporting. Administers payroll systems (e.g., Workday, ADP, OSV), audits payroll cycles, and verifies uploads to the general ledger. Researches, analyzes, and resolves payroll discrepancies, audit findings, and budget variances. Reviews payroll reports, responds to third-party payroll inquiries, and assists with worker’s compensation audits. Collaborates with cross-functional teams to support operational initiatives and organizational objectives. Fosters a collaborative, inclusive team environment while managing deadlines and shifting priorities. Actively seeks opportunities to influence, build effective relationships and gain alignment with peers, functional partners, and/or external partners to accomplish business objectives. Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the organization and oneself. Provides excellent positive customer service across an organizational structure and handles sensitive and confidential information with tact and discretion. Prioritizes time-critical assignments. Works independently and fosters a cooperative spirit within a large and/or small team of diverse cultures and experiences, while working in a fast-paced environment with multiple deadlines and frequently changing priorities. Perform other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsi bilities : Hire, train, mentor, and develop payroll staff members. Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Business Administration, Finance, or a related field required. Six (6) or more years of multi-state payroll experience in a high-volume environment required. Four (4) or more years of supervisory experience preferred An equivalent combination of education or experience may be accepted Experience with Workday required. Experience with One Source Virtual (OSV) preferred. Fundamental Payroll Certification (FPC) or Certified Payroll Professional (CPP) preferred. Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Strong knowledge of payroll processing and accounting principles in a high-volume organization. Solid understanding of payroll regulations, tax requirements, and labor laws. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Outlook) and payroll systems such as Workday, ADP, and OSV. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a focus on process improvement and operational efficiency. Actively seeks opportunities to influence, build effective relationships, and gain alignment with peers, functional partners, and/or external partners to accomplish business objectives. Accepts personal accountability, proactively seeks resolution for personal limitations head-on; and supports honesty and respect towards others, the company, and oneself. Develops new insights into situations; questions conventional approaches; encourages new ideas and innovations, designs and implements new or cutting-edge programs/processes.  Ability to generate and/or recognize imaginative or creative solutions that generate successful outcomes. Working knowledge of principles and practices of accounting and payroll processing and impact on general ledger within a large volume organization.  Basic knowledge of mandates and other regulations related to payroll processing and labor law, preferred. Location: Remote, USA Travel: Travel seldom required #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Instructional-Resources-Assistant---Federal-Work-Study_R20263588-1": {
      "title": "Instructional Resources Assistant - Federal Work Study",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: : $0.00 - $0.00 Must be a current National University student with a completed, current FAFSA. Position Summary The Federal Work Study position is a part-time, student worker opportunity with National University.  The student will provide general support and assistance to their selected department and will work on special projects as assigned and in alignment with the student’s stated interests and career goals. Essential Functions: Supports the development, curation, organization, and distribution of instructional resources for staff, faculty, and student use. Maintains training and attendance records, inputs data, and verifies that information is keyed accurately and in a timely manner. Creates and organizes analytical reports and presentations. Administrative and clerical duties; general office assistance. Requirements: Must be a current National University student who has completed a current FAFSA. Ability to work up to 25 hours per week with a varied schedule. Must be willing and able to handle material in a confidential manner.  Technical / Functional Skills : Exceptional verbal and written communication skills, with experience using Microsoft Office Suite. Excellent time management skills. Ability to understand and follow written and oral instructions. Ability to complete projects in a timely manner. Outstanding organizational and critical thinking skills. Collaborate effectively with a team of diverse cultures. Adaptable to work independently within a fast-paced environment with multiple deadlines and frequently changing priorities. #LI-DNI   Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold