    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Part-time-Faculty--BS-Computer-Science_R20263600-1": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, B.S. Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California   Part-time Faculty: B.S. Computer Science   Location: Hybrid – San Diego     National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC).   Job Description   The Department of Engineering, Data, and Computer Sciences, in the College of Business, Engineering and Technology at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty with a specialization in Computer Science. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of, or potential for excellence in, the following: teaching in their field, a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body, and related scholarship and/or research . This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success.   Essential Job Duties:   Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. undefined Qualifications: Required: Master’s degree in Computer Science or a closely related field. Must reside in and be legally authorized to work in the United States.   Preferred: PhD in computer science or related area. Industry experience. Teaching or training experience.   For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following.   A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body.   Salary and Compensation:   Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89   Successful candidates will receive offers on a salary/pay scale commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, experience, and competencies. Base pay is one component of the National University’s total rewards package.  Full details of benefit offerings can be found here .  Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Part-time-Faculty--School-Psychology_R20263587": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, School Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: School Psychology Location: Remote, USA National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Position Summary The Department of ASPEC-ABA, School Psychology, and Ed Counseling, in the Sanford College of Education at the National University invites applications for part-time faculty in School Psychology. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of or potential for excellence in teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Please note that in addition to a resume or CV, unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained are required at the time of application. If a candidate's school psychology credential was issued by a state other than California, candidates selected for hire must obtain a California Commission on Teacher Credentialling (CCTC) Pupil Personnel Services (PPS) credential within one year of hire.  Essential Job Duties Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications Required Master's degree in the field of school psychology/psychology from a regionally accredited university.  Minimum 5 years' experience as a practicing, credentialed school psychologist.  Current, state-issued credential in school psychology. If credential was issued by a state other than California, candidates selected for hire must obtain a California Commission on Teacher Credentialling (CCTC) Pupil Personnel Services (PPS) credential within one year of hire.  Knowledge and proficiency with the following assessments: Wechsler Intelligence Scale for Children® Fifth Edition (WISC®-V), Wechsler Individual Achievement Test® | Fourth Edition (WIAT-4), Kaufman Test of Educational Achievement Third Edition (KTEA™-3), Kaufman Assessment Battery for Children | Second Edition Normative Update (KABC™-II NU), Woodcock-Johnson® V (WJ V™).  Experience with iPad administration of assessments.  Available to teach Saturday Zoom Residency courses.  Preferred: 2 years of higher education teaching experience. Terminal degree in Psychology. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained. #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Records-and-Enrollment-Technician-I_R20263580": {
      "title": "Records and Enrollment Technician I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Hourly: $20.00 - $23.00 Position Summary This position is responsible for daily processes related to the Office of the Registrar and Student Records. The primary responsibilities include maintaining student records, timely processing of incoming transcripts, enrollment paperwork, and other documents pertaining to student records. Receives and fulfills requests for National University academic transcripts and transcripts for which National University is designated custodian of records. Receives and processes requests to verify enrollment and degree status. Assists in disseminating and enforcing admissions eligibility information and National University policies and procedures to students, faculty, and staff to ensure compliance. This position is also responsible for maintaining record integrity and upholding FERPA policy and compliance within administrative policies and procedures.      Essential Functions:     Document Processing and Student Record Maintenance  Receives and reviews enrollment documents and miscellaneous student records; verifies authenticity of incoming transcripts and miscellaneous documents. Maintains log of all incoming documents. Routes documents for processing to our document management system Hyland OnBase in a timely manner.   Verifies, indexes, and uploads scanned enrollment paperwork, transcripts, and other documents to the document management system with careful attention to creating clear and legible images. Updates the student information system with received status. Communicates with students and staff by disseminating information through relevant channels and posting pertinent materials.  Works with National Student Clearinghouse to verify complete student files, including all transcripts from transfer-eligible institutions to meet Basis for Admission requirements.   Reviews and maintains Grade Rosters and Attendance Rosters to assist Faculty and Center Directors with entering attendance into the student information system and posting official grades.  Reviews and processes Incomplete Grade Requests and Modifications, Grade Changes, Late Drop Requests, and Late Add Requests through the Student Information System. Ensures that the documents on file are in alignment and accurate with the Student Information System.  Other duties as assigned.  Answers incoming telephone calls and email inquiries from students, faculty and staff concerning the status of enrollment documentation, receipt of incoming transcripts, status of outgoing transcript orders, and accuracy of University enrollment and degree information.   Provides general information and refers callers to the appropriate staff or department for assistance.   Documents inquiries on student files via customer relationship management system and student information system.  As a primary contact to the University community, enforces and disseminates University policies and procedures to assure consistent and uniform application of regulations. Assists students and staff with issues or concerns regarding admission and eligibility, with issues or concerns regarding grades and/or attendance, enrollment and degree information, and with transcript orders to assure resolution of the problem or concern.  As a secondary contact for the University community, enforces Academic Standing, Satisfactory Academic Progress, graduation requirement policies, and University catalog information. Disseminates general University information related to students’ records.  Outgoing Transcripts and Letters    Daily maintenance and troubleshooting of transcripts orders received via Parchment transcript vendor.    Daily processing of Enrollment Verification requests received via Parchment.  Attendance Roster Maintenance  Coordinates the updates of in-class attendance in collaboration with Center Support Team, verifies University enrollment, and confirmation of degree status.   Grade Roster Maintenance  Reviews Grade Roster status and works with Faculty to ensure grade posting timelines are maintained. Assists with training faculty on grade inputting and approvals as needed.     Supervisory Responsibilities: N/A   Requirements:   Education & Experience  Associate’s degree or equivalent relevant experience preferred  Minimum one (1) year of experience in an office environment required, preferably in a higher education setting   Good understanding of file management required   Experience with any of the following programs: Hyland OnBase,  Hyland Brainware, Oracle CRM RightNowSalesforce, and SOAR PeopleSoft Anthology preferred.   Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills  Aptitude for organization, thoroughness, and accuracy in detailed work. Highly detailed oriented.   Ability to work near others in a congenial and supportive environment.    A bility to work independently and under pressure of deadlines.    Possess mature judgment with ability to be tactful and diplomatic in difficult student and staff/faculty encounters, good oral and interpersonal communication skills.    Ability to identify and solve problems.   General knowledge of Microsoft Windows and Office Suite.  Knowledge of Adobe Acrobat Pro for creating and editing PDFs preferred. Proficient knowledge of computer uses and software packages; preference given to applicants with demonstrated experience/expertise with Windows 10.  Experience with document scanning and management and student information systems preferred.        Location: Remote Hybrid/San Diego California Travel: No Travel Required Participates in a rotating onsite schedule, working from the San Diego office two days approximately every 5–6 weeks to process and manage physical incoming mail, including transcripts and other student documents.    #LI-Hybrid Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Senior-Manager--Conversion-Rate-Optimization_R20263594": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Conversion Rate Optimization",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $78,496.00 - $105,974.00 Position Summary: The Senior Manager, Experimentation & Optimization leads conversion rate optimization (CRO) and experimentation for National University’s website and Digital experiences. This is a strategic, data-driven role responsible for defining and executing the CRO roadmap, proactively identifying optimization opportunities, and improving website experiences based on prospective student behavior, user insights, performance data, and lifecycle stage. The primary goal is to increase inquiry, application, and enrollment conversion through data-informed testing, continuous optimization, and an improved user experience. Essential Functions: CRO Strategy & Roadmap Own the CRO and experimentation roadmap for NU’s website and Digital experiences including opportunity identification, intake, prioritization, sequencing and the testing calendar. Define, execute, and continuously optimize data-driven testing and optimization strategies that improve user experience, engagement, conversion, and content relevance across prospect-facing web experiences. Own website experimentation roadmap, related platform strategy, and associated vendor/partner relationships. Establish testing SLAs, QA standards, governance, and deployment practices that prevent conflicts across concurrent tests, campaigns, and releases. Maintain a repository of hypotheses, test results, learnings, optimization opportunities, and best practices that accelerate knowledge sharing and continuous improvement.   Experimentation & Proactive A/B Testing Own the complete experimentation lifecycle: opportunity identification, hypothesis development, prioritization, test design, implementation, QA, launch, measurement, readout, and production rollout of winners. Proactively source the testing pipeline from behavioral analytics, session data, UX research, and website funnel diagnostics rather than operating as a request-driven queue. Design and run A/B, multivariate, and multi-page experiments, ensuring appropriate sample sizing, run length, and statistical significance before a result is acted on. Optimize information architecture, content presentation, navigation, page experience, and calls-to-action using customer insight and behavioral data. Translate experimentation outcomes into optimization recommendations that inform future website roadmaps, experience strategy, and investment priorities.   Journey Discovery and Experience Optimization Analyze the end-to-end prospective student journey to identify friction, abandonment, and conversion opportunities using behavioral analytics, session replay, UX research, and customer feedback. Champion continuous optimization of program discovery across web properties, including on-site search, filters, navigation, program finders, and recommendation surfaces. Develop targeted website experience strategies using established audience segments, intent signals, engagement patterns, lifecycle stage, and experimentation insights to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion. Develop and optimize personalized website experiences that deliver relevant messaging, content, navigation, and recommendations based on audience needs, behavioral insights, and lifecycle stage. Partner with Marketing, Enrollment, and Digital Analytics to leverage audience segments, first-party customer data, and behavioral insights to support website personalization and optimization initiatives. Identify opportunities to apply AI-assisted optimization, predictive insights, and behavioral decisioning to improve relevance, engagement, and conversion outcomes. Participate and input into Journey Operations that impact Prospect Student experience in partnership with IT, Accounts, Brand and Product teams.   Measurement, KPIs & Reporting Cadence Own measurement best practices, quarterly meta-analysis, CRO Playbook, dashboards, and the KPI framework supporting CRO, experimentation, and website personalization efforts. Define, monitor, and communicate KPIs including experimentation velocity, win rate, conversion improvement, inquiry conversion, application progression, website conversion, journey completion, personalization effectiveness, and incremental business impact. Establish and maintain a regular reporting cadence, including weekly program status, monthly CRO performance readouts, and quarterly roadmap and business-impact reviews for senior leadership. Build executive dashboards and communicate test results, KPI trends, roadmap progress, and strategic recommendations to the Chief Marketing Officer and senior stakeholders. Partner with the Digital Analytics team to establish analytical requirements, measurement plans, and dashboard reporting for UX. Measure the maturity of National University’s experimentation program and continuously evolve optimization capabilities through data-driven insight.     Innovation & Continuous Improvement Evaluate emerging trends in AI, personalization, experimentation, behavioral science, and digital experience optimization. Identify opportunities to incorporate intelligent personalization, predictive experiences, and innovative optimization capabilities into National University’s prospective student website experiences. Evaluate new technologies, platforms, and optimization capabilities that strengthen website audience engagement, experience effectiveness, and conversion performance. Continuously benchmark industry trends, competitor experiences, customer expectations, and evolving digital behaviors to identify future opportunities for innovation and growth. Other duties as assigned.   Supervisory Responsi bilities: Individual contributor role that provides leadership through influence and expertise; scope may evolve over time based on organizational needs.   Requirements: Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, Business, Analytics, Statistics, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field. Master’s degree or M.B.A. preferred. 7 + years of experience in conversion rate optimization and experimentation, website experience management, personalization, digital merchandising, or e-commerce. 2+ years of experience in a strategy, program ownership, or related manager responsibilities. Demonstrated ownership and administration of A/B testing and personalization platforms (Adobe Target, VWO, Optimizely, or equivalent), including governance, implementation oversight, and optimization best practices. Experience designing, implementing, and optimizing personalized digital experiences using audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, geo-targeting, and journey-based experience targeting. Proven experience developing and executing a CRO and experimentation roadmap, including KPI development, prioritization frameworks, and executive reporting. Experience managing vendors, agency partners, and external development resources to deliver experimentation, personalization, and digital optimization initiatives. Demonstrated track record of leveraging experimentation and personalization strategies to drive measurable improvements in conversion, lead generation, engagement, and business outcomes. Experience in higher education, edtech, or another complex, high-consideration, multi-audience environment preferred. Portfolio, case studies, or documented examples demonstrating measurable conversion improvements and successful optimization initiatives across complex digital ecosystems.   Competencies/Technical/Functional Skills: Deep expertise in experimentation methodologies, including hypothesis development, test design, statistical analysis, and interpretation of results to support business decisions. Strong experience leading conversion rate optimization (CRO), personalization, and digital experience optimization programs at scale. Expertise with experimentation, personalization, and analytics platforms such as Adobe Target, Optimizely, VWO, Adobe Analytics, GA4, and FullStory. Strong understanding of customer data platforms, audience segmentation, behavioral targeting, and customer journey optimization. Ability to independently analyze, validate, and interpret complex datasets using SQL, dashboards, and analytics tools to identify opportunities and inform strategy. Experience developing experimentation roadmaps, success metrics, governance processes, and executive reporting frameworks. Strong understanding of UX principles, customer journey mapping, and the integration of qualitative and quantitative insights into optimization strategies. Knowledge of accessibility (WCAG), responsive design principles, content strategy, and technical considerations impacting experimentation and personalization. Experience evaluating and applying emerging technologies, including AI-driven personalization, predictive modeling, and automated decisioning. Exceptional communication, storytelling, stakeholder management, and executive presentation skills, with the ability to translate data into actionable business recommendations. Demonstrated ability to influence and build alignment across Marketing, Product, UX, Technology, Analytics, Enrollment, and other cross-functional teams without direct authority. Strategic mindset with the ability to balance long-term vision, customer needs, operational realities, and measurable business outcomes while driving complex initiatives to completion.    Location: Remote, USA   Travel: up to 10% travel #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. The minimum salary will be offered based on the minimum exemption threshold based on state of residency. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For Part-time benefits, please click here . National University is committed to maintaining a high-quality workforce representative of the populations we serve. National University employs more than 4,500 faculty and staff and serves over 45,000 students. We are united in our mission to meet the global education demands of the 21st Century and are dedicated to creating a supportive academic and work environment that allows students, faculty and staff to develop their interests and talents while experiencing a sense of community. With programs available both online and at our many campus locations, National University is a leader in creating innovative solutions to education and meeting the needs of our student population, including adult learners and working professionals. National University (NU) is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
    },
    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Remote-USA/Part-time-Faculty--Clinical-Mental-Health-Counseling_R20263513": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: Annual Salary: $26.63 - $28.89 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Clinical Mental Health Counseling Location: Remote, USA National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Please note that in addition to a resume or CV, unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained are required at the time of application. Position Summary The Department of Social Work, in the JFK School of Psychology and Social Sciences at National University, invites applications for part-time faculty in Clinical Mental Health Counseling. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of, or potential for excellence in, teaching in their field and a commitment to serving the University’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Essential Job Duties Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications Required Doctorate degree with focus in Counseling and Supervision or related counseling field from a regionally accredited institution. Minimum two (2) years of direct teaching experience at the Master and/or Doctoral level. Three plus (3+) years of professional and/or research experience in Educational Leadership. Must have personal computer and ability to facilitate online instruction and communications remotely. Graduate of CACREP-approved program. Preferred Curriculum development experience. Research-based, scholarly, peer-reviewed journal article publications. Experience guiding students through the dissertation process. Experience in higher education. Experience working in a technology-driven enterprise. For full consideration, interested candidates must provide the following: Resume or CV. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained. #LI-Remote Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make the impact of a lifetime for each of our student learners. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment, education, and admission at National University."
