    "https://nus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/Spectrum-Center-San-Diego-CA/Part-time-Faculty--Fingerprinting-Analysis_R20263563": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, Fingerprinting Analysis",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nPart time\n\nCompensation Range: : $0.00 - $0.00 National University – San Diego, California Part-time Faculty: Fingerprinting Analysis Location: Onsite – Spectrum (San Diego, CA) National University is a veteran-founded, San Diego-based nonprofit. Since 1971, our mission has been to provide accessible higher education to adult learners. Today, we educate a diverse student body from across the U.S. and around the globe, with more than 230,000 alumni worldwide.  Our three schools and three colleges offer more than 200 accredited and licensed graduate and undergraduate programs. National University holds accreditation through the Western Senior College and Universities Commission (WSCUC). Job Description The School of Public Service at National University invites applications for part-time faculty in Fingerprinting Analysis. The successful candidate will have a demonstrated record of / or potential for excellence in teaching in both fields and a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. The successful candidate will have the potential for a commitment to serving the university’s diverse adult student body. This position primarily works closely with the Academic Program Director and other faculty within the program and contributes to ensuring program quality, student engagement, and success. Essential Job Duties: Lead classroom sessions onsite. Provide expertise in assigned content area by maintaining current knowledge in the field. Provide substantive, timely feedback to students on various assessment activities. Maintain a positive, safe, inclusive student-centric learning environment. Complete required tasks on deadlines (e.g., final grades, assessment, grading rubrics, input for grade appeals, etc.) Maintain appropriate professional training and/or scholarly activities, when applicable. Provide feedback to the course lead regarding the course content. Identify at-risk students and collaborate with student services. Qualifications: Doctoral degree in the criminal justice, forensic science, or related field preferred. Minimum of 2 years of experience with performing fingerprint comparisons and analysis required. Minimum of 1 year of higher education teaching adult learner experience preferred. Experience working in Law Enforcement preferred. Experience in developing course content preferred. Must be eligible to work in California to facilitate courses onsite at the Spectrum Campus in San Diego. For full consideration, interested candidates should provide the following: A cover letter. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree attained. A curriculum vita. Statement of teaching experience online and/or onsite for a diverse student body. Salary and Compensation: Hourly: $26.63 - $28.89 Successful candidates will receive offers on a salary/pay scale commensurate with the candidate's qualifications, experience, and competencies. Base pay is one component of the National University’s total rewards package.   Full details of benefit offerings can be found here . #LI-ONSITE Candidate receiving offers will be offered a salary/pay rate commensurate with experience that vary based on a candidate’s qualifications, skills, and competencies.  Absent exceptional circumstances, candidates will be offered a salary within this range for this position. Base pay is one component of National University’s total rewards package, as we are dedicated to supporting the needs of the “whole you” with our holistic approach to employee benefits by offering comprehensive well-being benefits for you and your family.  For full details about our benefit plan offerings, please visit benefits.nu.edu . For part-time positions, please click here . National University is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any employee or applicant per applicable federal, state and local laws. At NU, a mix of highly talented, innovative, and creative people come together to make